WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.803
-The President held an impromptu
press conference today,

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.372
lashing out at Democrats
calling for his impeachment.

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:08.941
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:13.546
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.214
This morning, Democratic leaders

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:17.149
were scheduled to meet
with Trump at the White House

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:18.451
about infrastructure.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.553
Now, why the Democrats
were meeting with him at all

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.587
is beyond me.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.122
First of all,
he's never kept his word

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:24.924
on any promise
he's ever made to them,

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.625
and, second,
he's fighting Congress

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:29.428
on literally every front
related to their investigation.

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:32.198
In fact, before the meeting,
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi,

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.300
who's facing increasing calls
from her own caucus

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.604
to impeach Trump, accused him
of orchestrating a cover-up.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.672
-We believe
that no one is above the law,

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.741
including the president
of the United States.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.876
And we believe that the
president of the United States

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:46.079
is engaged in a cover-up.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:48.714
-Yeah, he is.
So why are you meeting with him?

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:50.883
That's like responding
to someone's birthday e-vite

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:54.120
by writing, "I resent
the day you were born,"

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.190
and then still clicking,
"Will attend."

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.527
Now, it will not surprise you
to learn that Trump

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.262
did not take kindly
to that remark,

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:05.465
and shortly afterward, he called
an impromptu press conference.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:08.234
And you knew right off the bat
this was gonna be a weird one,

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.236
because before Trump
even got there,

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.439
he had a sign printed up
in front of the podium

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:15.307
with the words "No collusion"
and "No obstruction" on it.

00:01:15.307 --> 00:01:17.510
First of all,
this is such a dumb sign

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.246
because he made
the words "No" super big

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.881
and the other words super tiny.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.349
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.786
I have a feeling the staff at
D.C. Kinkos voted for Hillary.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.221
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:32.959
If anything, this looks like the
least effective anti-drug PSA.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:35.128
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:37.163
And sure enough --
sure enough --

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.598
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:42.101
Trump's press conference
was predictably off the rails.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.602
He started out
with an obvious lie

00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:45.838
that he just assumed
everyone else would agree with.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:49.108
-I just saw that Nancy Pelosi
just before our meeting

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:50.776
made a statement that
"We believe that

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:53.112
the president
of the United States

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:55.414
is engaged in a cover-up."

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:57.550
Well, it turns out
I'm the most --

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.718
and I think most of you
would agree to this.

00:01:59.718 --> 00:02:02.889
I'm the most
transparent president

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:04.991
probably in the history
of this country.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:07.026
-No, we would not agree.
I mean...

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.561
[ Laughter ]
I mean, we could see

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.297
right through you, but I don't
think that's what you meant.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.600
He always tries --
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.636
He does this thing
where he always tries

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:20.206
to trick everybody into thinking
they agree with them.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:23.242
He's like a guy on a first date
who tries to sneak in something

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.845
like, "So, I think you'd agree,
we should go back to my place,"

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.514
and you're like, "Uh, you
haven't been reading the signs."

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.282
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:32.785
Trump then complained
about the hearings and subpoenas

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.354
issued by the chairman of the
House Judiciary Committee,

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:37.123
Jerry Nadler,
who's from New York.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.924
Trump's administration
has repeatedly obstructed

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:41.127
Nadler's investigation
and defied his subpoenas,

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.428
and Trump complained
about Nadler

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.729
during his press conference.

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:46.065
-Jerry Nadler, who's been
an enemy of mine for many years,

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:49.102
he fought me in New York --
unsuccessfully, by the way.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.704
I've had great success
against Jerry.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.105
-"Great success against Jerry?"

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:56.776
You know you're the bad guy when
you literally sound like Newman.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.978
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.247
So, Trump is now
openly defying the law

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.714
and refusing
to work with Congress

00:03:02.714 --> 00:03:04.216
unless they stop
investigating him.

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:06.686
It's worth remembering
that Republicans spent years

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.687
pretending to care
about the Constitution,

00:03:08.687 --> 00:03:11.223
and now Trump
is exposing them all as frauds.

00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:13.325
In fact, during the campaign,
Trump pretended that he, too,

00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:14.994
was concerned
about government overreach

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:18.197
and that all he wanted to do was
get back to the Constitution.

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:22.601
-It's all about
the Constitution of -- of --

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.872
And so important,
the Constitution,

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:28.341
the way it was meant to be.

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.443
I'm a very strong
Constitutionalist.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:32.077
I mean,
I feel so strongly about it.

00:03:32.077 --> 00:03:37.483
The mainstream media wants
to surrender our Constitution.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:40.286
I feel very strongly
about our Constitution.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.587
I'm proud of it.
I love it.

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:43.622
And I want
to go through the Constitution.

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:44.824
That's what we want to do.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:47.860
I mean, we want to bring
the Constitution back.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.561
-What do you mean bring it back?

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:51.697
He talks about the Constitution

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:54.367
like he's rebooting
a classic TV show on Netflix.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.835
We want to bring "Friends" back,

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.971
and this time, there's gonna be
a lot more Marcel.

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:01.273
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:04.143
Trump was just echoing years
of empty Republican rhetoric

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.678
about respecting
the Constitution,

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.780
and this week, we got to see
just how empty and meaningless

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.216
all that rhetoric was
when one Republican,

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.451
Michigan Congressman
Justin Amash,

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:14.087
became the first member
of his party in Congress

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.521
to call for Trump's impeachment.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:18.291
Amash laid out his reasoning
in an extensive Twitter thread

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:19.792
where he cited
the Mueller report

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:22.228
and the Constitution's
section on impeachment and wrote

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.230
"Our Constitution
is brilliant and awesome.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.965
It deserves a government
to match it."

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.299
And instead of celebrating him

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:28.567
as a champion
of the Constitution,

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.102
his fellow Republicans
slammed him.

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:32.905
Trump even took to Twitter
to call Amash a loser.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:35.208
And when Amash was asked about
Trump's comments on the street,

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:37.243
his answer was simple
yet effective.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:40.647
-Sir, what about President Trump
calling you a loser?

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:41.880
-Okay.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.716
-Honestly --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:45.818
Honestly, yeah.
I mean...

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:49.722
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:52.391
That probably
is the best way to respond.

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:53.959
You know, just treat him
like he's a grandpa

00:04:53.959 --> 00:04:55.094
in the nursing home.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:57.029
"The nurses
are stealing my pills,

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:59.732
and they want
to sell my organs to Mexico."

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.701
"Okay."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.336
So, instead of joining Amash
and actually

00:05:04.336 --> 00:05:05.838
reading the Constitution,

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:07.906
Republicans are standing with
Trump as he stonewalls Congress

00:05:07.906 --> 00:05:09.175
and openly defies the law.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.544
For example, the Trump
administration is refusing

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:14.180
to comply with a subpoena
to release Trump's tax returns.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.115
Now, "The Washington Post"
reported this week

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.418
that a confidential draft memo
from the IRS

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:20.953
said the tax returns
must be given to Congress

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.155
unless the President
invokes executive privilege.

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:25.958
And yet during a hearing today,
Treasury Secretary Steve Mnuchin

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:28.461
insisted the President was right
not to release them,

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.429
and also
that he had nothing to hide.

00:05:30.429 --> 00:05:34.066
-Do you think the American
people have a right to know

00:05:34.066 --> 00:05:36.235
what's in those tax forms?

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.971
-No, I don't.
Presidents are not required to,

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.806
and the American public

00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:43.375
knew that he didn't release them
before they voted for him.

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:46.312
-Do you know
what the President's hiding?

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.379
-Can you repeat that?
I'm sorry.

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:49.415
-Do you know what he's hiding?

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:52.018
He doesn't want anybody
to see them, so...

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:53.886
-I don't think
he's hiding anything.

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:56.589
-Yeah, no, he is.
I mean, when you have something

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.491
and you won't let people see it,
that's hiding.

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:01.494
That's what that word means
on our planet.

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:02.628
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:04.163
Also, Trump's
always hiding something.

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.965
He spent his entire life
lying about everything

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:07.366
from his net worth
to his businesses

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:08.467
to his personal life.

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:09.868
If we subpoenaed
his driver's license,

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:11.870
we'd probably find out
his real name was something

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:14.273
totally different,
like Tidally D. Wigglesmith III.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:20.913
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:22.982
I hadn't noticed the picture
the first time.

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:25.450
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.587
"Are you good with the picture?"
"No, that looks great."

00:06:27.587 --> 00:06:28.887
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.887 --> 00:06:30.756
And not only is Trump
hiding his tax returns,

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:33.025
he's also telling his aides
not to comply with requests

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.360
to testify before Congress.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:35.594
This week, for example,
he ordered

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:37.563
his former White House counsel
Don McGahn

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:40.565
to defy a subpoena and skip
a hearing on the Mueller report,

00:06:40.565 --> 00:06:42.868
three weeks after Trump's
Attorney General William Barr

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:44.670
also refused to show up
for a hearing,

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.039
which means we've now had
two congressional hearings

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:49.908
in three weeks with members
talking to empty chairs.

00:06:49.908 --> 00:06:52.644
And you know things are bad
when C-SPAN is getting attention

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:56.048
for shots of empty chairs,
because C-SPAN specializes

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:58.117
in shots of empty chairs.

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:00.719
Whenever you see a close shot of
a member of Congress like this,

00:07:00.719 --> 00:07:02.722
it looks like they're talking to
a bunch of their colleagues

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:04.123
until they take the wide shot...

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:05.157
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.157 --> 00:07:06.525
...and you see
that no one's there.

00:07:06.525 --> 00:07:07.626
I mean, look at that.

00:07:07.626 --> 00:07:08.995
That looks like
a college lecture hall

00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:10.796
during a class
no one wanted to take.

00:07:10.796 --> 00:07:14.233
You know, something like Geology
in the age of Social Media.

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:15.568
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:17.169
Democrats want McGahn to testify

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:18.804
because he's a key witness
in the Mueller report

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:21.207
and he has evidence about some
of the most damning accusations

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:23.075
of obstruction of justice
against Trump.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:25.478
For example, McGahn said Trump
ordered him to fire Mueller

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:27.079
in the middle
of the investigation,

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:28.881
but McGahn refused,
threatening to quit.

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:31.216
And in doing so,
he used some colorful language

00:07:31.216 --> 00:07:34.286
that news anchors have been
happy to repeat on air.

00:07:34.286 --> 00:07:36.255
McGahn spoke with
the president twice

00:07:36.255 --> 00:07:39.257
and understood the directive
the same way both times.

00:07:39.257 --> 00:07:42.828
In response to that request,
McGahn decided to quit.

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:45.097
He called a lawyer,
drove to the White House,

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:47.900
packed up his office, prepared
to submit a resignation letter

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.770
with his chief of staff,
told Reince Priebus

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.506
that the President had asked him
"to do crazy [bleep]"

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:55.807
-Don McGahn
says to Reince Priebus,

00:07:55.807 --> 00:07:58.176
which is the third witness
to this incident,

00:07:58.176 --> 00:08:01.714
"The President asked me
to do some crazy [bleep]"

00:08:01.714 --> 00:08:03.915
-If there's one thing
we can be grateful for

00:08:03.915 --> 00:08:05.384
in this otherwise horrible time

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:08.454
it's straight-laced news anchors
just letting loose.

00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:10.022
Used to be,
you'd tune in to the news,

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:11.790
and Walter Kronkite
would solemnly read

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.659
the day's headlines,
and now journalists

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:15.995
are like drunk Red Sox fans
lighting cars on fire

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:17.196
after the World Series.

00:08:17.196 --> 00:08:19.398
"[Bleep] hey, bro,
that's some crazy [bleep]"

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:20.432
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.432 --> 00:08:22.134
I mean, pretty soon...

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:27.239
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:27.239 --> 00:08:28.540
At this rate, pretty soon,

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:32.011
MSNBC is gonna have a show
just called [Bleep]

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:37.049
[ Laughter ]

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:44.590
-Welcome to "[Bleep]."

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.959
[ Laughter ]

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:49.428
It's like when the redacted
Mueller report first came out

00:08:49.428 --> 00:08:50.962
and Wolf Blitzer
read Trump's

00:08:50.962 --> 00:08:53.633
expletive-filled response
on national television.

00:08:53.633 --> 00:08:56.068
-This is what the President
himself said,

00:08:56.068 --> 00:09:01.040
and I'm quoting him now.
He calls it "Total [bleep]"

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.009
-It's so bizarre to see someone
say those words

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:05.511
in such a dry tone.

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:08.013
It's like
an episode of "Star Trek"

00:09:08.013 --> 00:09:10.549
where they give Data
a profanity chip.

00:09:10.549 --> 00:09:12.984
"Captain, I've detected
a goddamn anomaly

00:09:12.984 --> 00:09:14.653
in the [bleep] warp core,
bitch."

00:09:14.653 --> 00:09:16.956
[ Laughter ]

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:19.525
We need to hear from McGahn,

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:20.893
we need to hear
from Robert Mueller,

00:09:20.893 --> 00:09:22.528
and we need to hear again
from Barr,

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:23.996
who's basically been threatening

00:09:23.996 --> 00:09:26.165
to turn the Justice Department
into a political weapon

00:09:26.165 --> 00:09:28.067
to be wielded against
the President's opponents.

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:29.735
Last week,
Barr appointed a prosecutor

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:31.603
to examine the origins
of the Russia probe.

00:09:31.603 --> 00:09:33.939
And at a rally on Monday,
Trump responded to chants

00:09:33.939 --> 00:09:35.407
of "Lock them up"
by telling the crowd

00:09:35.407 --> 00:09:37.343
his Attorney General
would look into it.

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:40.513
-This phony witch hunt that
we all went through together,

00:09:40.513 --> 00:09:42.414
it's a disgrace.

00:09:42.414 --> 00:09:45.117
If that ever happened
to the other side,

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:47.954
this thing would've been over
two years ago.

00:09:47.954 --> 00:09:49.622
And you know,
it would've been treason.

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:51.457
They would've called it treason.

00:09:51.457 --> 00:09:53.926
And that's what it is --
it was treason.

00:09:53.926 --> 00:09:58.297
-Lock them up! Lock them up!
Lock them up!

00:09:58.297 --> 00:10:01.133
-Well, we have a great new
Attorney General

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:03.869
who's gonna give it
a very fair look.

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:05.905
-If an angry mob chants
"Lock them up"

00:10:05.905 --> 00:10:07.940
about your political opponents,
the proper response isn't

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:08.974
"We'll give it a look."

00:10:08.974 --> 00:10:10.509
That's how a mechanic responds

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:12.044
when you ask them
to check your motor oil.

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:14.313
"We'll give it a look.
It'll cost $2,000."

00:10:14.313 --> 00:10:17.048
And then you say,
"$2,000 for motor oil?

00:10:17.048 --> 00:10:19.785
That's..."
-Total [bleep]

00:10:19.785 --> 00:10:21.453
This has been
